<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Morning-Light.jpg" alt="Painting of a landscape with sheep in the foreground" width="500" height="398" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">Morning Light. 16x20, oil on linen. 2014.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I started work on this painting two months ago and left it hanging unfinished on my studio wall before revisiting the design and adding the sheep this week. &nbsp;I spent a few hours on the sheep and additional layers of glazing and scumbling to bring it close to completion.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">After letting everything dry I put some retouch varnish on the dark areas and decided against doing any more rework.</p>